A||||5||Optimusmc||85 SE won't start
Z||000000||Optimusmc||07-06-99||08:39 PM||||Please help! My car battery died on me and ever since I've been having problems. The latest(after replacing the battery) is that when starting the engine will rotate, but not start. I got it to start once by priming the engine and it ran fine after that(until I tried to start it later) Now there is no spark! I am getting power to the ignition coil, but no spark out. Replaced the ECM to no avail.  HELP!
Z||000001||Optimusmc||07-06-99||09:10 PM||||I forgot, I did check the coil and it is fine
Z||000002||theogre||07-06-99||10:03 PM||||first the "obviouse"........... find and disconnect the tach filter... it's usuallt a small can mounted near the thermostat on the 4 cyl. I don't know where on a 6. If that item is bad it will cause a no spark. the car will run without it.<p>you may also have fried the module on the distributor. the module controls spark while cranking and thru 600 RPM.
Z||000003||Optimusmc||07-06-99||10:53 PM||||ty for the help ogre, but that did not help. I did notice that while there is no fuel coming out when the battery is fully charged, and the Tach doesn't move that when the battery dies down and the engine chugs, there is fuel and the tach does move. Would this be attributed to the module?
Z||000004||wayne||07-07-99||11:04 AM||||I had this same type problem with my sons 85 GT. It about drove me crazy. There was never any rime or reason for it. you might wait 5 minutes or somtimes longer and it would run again.  I tried replacing just the module things which helped for a while but then started doing it again.  I final replaced the whole distributer about 9 months ago and so far has not done it again.<p>Of course I'll probalble get a phone call in a little while from my son telling me it's broke again.<p>hope this helps<p>wayne
Z||000005||Optimusmc||07-08-99||12:30 AM||||Thanks for the help. Replaced the module and now it starts right up!
